WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.500
Rutherford's atomic model was quite commendable

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.300
when it came to explaining the structure of atoms.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:14.320
However, it was not very appropriate theoretically.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.480
And why are we saying so?

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.960
We know that any charged object

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.600
which revolves in a circular motion gains acceleration gradually.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.620
Similarly, if the electron is moving fast in a circular path,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.500
then it will also gain acceleration.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.780
And on gaining acceleration,

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.860
it's bound to liberate energy in some form.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.280
Now if it continuously keeps radiating energy,

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.220
then ultimately all the energy of the electron

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.720
will get over and it will fall into the nucleus.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.540
This would result in high instability of the atom.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:53.440
But wait a second, all these things do not happen in an atom.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.580
And how do we know this?

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:59.360
Because in nature all the atoms are stable.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:04.260
That means the hypothesis put forth by Rutherford was also incorrect?

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.460
Not really!

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.460
The hypothesis just needed slight modifications.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:11.720
These were made by the next legendary scientist in our list,

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.780
called Neils Bohr.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.200
He made a few additional explanations

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:18.600
to describe the atomic structure.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.140
The postulates put forward by Neils Bohr were as follows.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.820
Firstly, only certain special orbits called

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:30.620
discrete orbits of electrons are allowed inside the atom.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.240
Secondly, while revolving in these discrete orbits,

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.980
the electrons do not radiate energy.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.680
Now these points definitely tell us why an atom is so stable.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.000
But what exactly are these paths

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.840
or orbits in which the electrons revolve around the nucleus?

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.480
Let's understand with an example!

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.500
Do you know how our solar system is?

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.360
Yes, it appears somewhat like this.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.560
Now here the sun is stationary at the center

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.880
while the planets revolve around it.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:06.680
But have you noticed that the planets always revolve in fixed paths?

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.080
We never find any planet jumping to

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.840
a different path all of a sudden, right?

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:15.780
They always encircle the sun in defined paths.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:19.020
In a similar way, we have the atomic structure.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.220
The nucleus acts like the sun located at the center.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.220
And the electrons are like planets which revolve in fixed, defined orbitals.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.540
These electron orbitals are referred to as shells or energy levels.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:36.980
Now the name energy levels gets us to an important concept.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:41.380
Neils Bohr suggested that the electrons revolving in these orbitals

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:43.380
do not radiate energy.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:47.100
Now this is justified when we use the term energy levels.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:51.840
Because it indicates that each shell has got a defined energy level.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:55.060
That means when the electrons revolve in these shells,

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:57.840
they do not liberate any form of energy.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:01.900
And how do we name these shells to indicate their position?

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.300
It's simple!

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.540
Beginning from the one near the nucleus

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.380
we name them as the 'K shell',

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:11.220
'L shell', 'M shell', 'N shell' and so on.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.920
Yes K,L,M,N and so on .

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:17.680
And what if we want to number them?

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.300
In that case we use the letter 'n' in lower case

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:27.320
and write them as 'n equals 1', 'n equals 2' , 'n equals 3' and so on

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.820
beginning from the one next to the nucleus.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:34.320
So we can name them alphabetically or we can even number them.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.280
With all these theories and points known,

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:40.920
do we now know the structure of a typical atom completely?

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:44.700
The nucleus contains positive protons and the electrons

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.620
revolving around in fixed orbitals.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.100
Is that how an atom is structured?

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:54.420
Not really! We still have one more subatomic particle left.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.920
And what and where could it be?

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:58.820
Let's find that out!

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.080
It was around the year 1932

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.220
when a famous English physicist

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:06.920
Sir James Chadwick found the third subatomic particle.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.400
He found that the particle had a mass

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.080
almost equivalent to that of the proton.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.360
And what about its charge?

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.720
Astonishingly it had no charge.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.720
Yes! The particle was neutral.

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:22.620
The particle was later named as neutron,

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.040
denoted by the letter 'n'.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:28.860
Thus now we have the complete design of an atom.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.540
In the center lies the nucleus having positively charged protons

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.140
and neutral neutrons,

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.440
while the negatively charged electrons

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.360
revolve in fixed orbitals around the nucleus.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.740
But how exactly are the electrons

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:45.540
distributed in the respective orbitals?

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.700
Is there a way to find out the maximum number of electrons

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.940
that one orbital can contain?

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:55.420
Or is it that the electrons are randomly scattered in the orbitals?

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:59.960
Let's find out the answers to these questions in our upcoming video.

